      "title": "Goyal leads biz delegation to Japan to discuss ways to boost trade",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/goyal-leads-biz-delegation-to-japan-to-discuss-ways-to-boost-trade-126082300458_1.html",
      "description": "Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal is leading a 200-member business delegation to Japan for a four-day visit starting August 24 to discuss ways to boost trade and investment ties between the two countries.\nThe visit assumes significance as Japan last year set an investment target of 10 trillion yen (about Rs 60,000 cr) in India over a decade.\nThe minister will be travelling to Tokyo, Nagoya and Osaka.\nThe business delegation has representatives from various sectors, ranging from manufacturing, semiconductors, clean energy and steel to automotive, financial services, healthcare and start-ups, industry chamber Ficci Director General Jyoti Viz told reporters here.\nIn Tokyo, Goyal will hold a series of meetings with the top leadership of major Japanese conglomerates and industrial houses that have long been partners in India's growth, alongside a round-table with Keidanren (Japan Business Federation), representing over 1,500 leading Japanese companies.\nDedicated sessions are",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-23T12:28:35"
    }
